Aapke paas packages ka ek sequence hai (conveyor belt pe line me pade hue).
Har package ka weight diya hai. weights = [w1, w2, w3, ...] 
Aapke paas ek ship hai jo har din ek trip karegi.

Rules (bahut important) Har din ship load hoti hai Conveyor belt ke starting se or Order change nahi kar sakte or 
Ship ki ek fixed max capacity hoti hai or Ek din me jitna load hua, us din ka total weight ≤ capacity Packages split nahi kar sakte 
Ek package ek hi din me poora load hoga or Aapko sab packages ko exactly days ke andar ship karna hai

#Aapko kya find karna hai? => Ship ki minimum possible capacity jisse sab packages days ke andar ship ho jaayein

STEP 1️⃣ : Binary Search ka matlab kya hai? Binary Search ka matlab:
Answer pe search karna, elements pe nahi
Is question me hum capacity dhoondh rahe hain. To hum capacity ke range pe search karte hain.

STEP 2️⃣ : LOW (starting) kyun ye hota hai?
low = max(weights)
❓ Kyun?
Socho: Ek package ka weight = 10
Agar capacity = 5
Kya ship kar paoge? ❌
👉 Matlab capacity isse chhoti ho hi nahi sakti
🧠 LOW = minimum possible answer

STEP 3️⃣ : HIGH (ending) kyun ye hota hai?
high = sum(weights)
❓ Kyun?
Socho: Saare packages ek hi din me bhej do
To capacity = sabka total weight
👉 Isse zyada capacity ki kabhi zarurat hi nahi
🧠 HIGH = maximum possible answer

STEP 4️⃣ : MID ka matlab (sabse important 🔥)
mid = (low + high) / 2;
MID ka matlab: “Bhai, agar capacity = MID ho to kya kaam ho jaayega?”
Is capacity me days ke andar ship ho gaya
Socho:
“Agar itni capacity chal rahi hai
to shayad thodi kam bhi chal jaaye”


class Solution {
public:
    bool possible(vector<int>& weights, int capicity, int days){
        int n = weights.size();
        int count = 1;
        int sum = 0;

        for(int i=0; i<n; i++){
            if(sum + weights[i] <= capicity){
                sum = sum + weights[i];
            }
            else{
                count++;
                sum = weights[i];   
            }
        }
        if(count <= days){
            return true;
        }
        else{
            return false;
        }
    }
    int shipWithinDays(vector<int>& weights, int days) {
        int n = weights.size();
        int start = *max_element(weights.begin(), weights.end());
        int end = accumulate(weights.begin(), weights.end(), 0);
        int ans = end;

        while(start <= end){
            int mid = start +  (end - start)/2;
            if(possible(weights, mid, days)){
                ans = mid;
                end = mid - 1;
            }
            else{
                start = mid + 1;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
};
